# kldload dnf5 boot-environment snapshot — libdnf5 "actions" plugin rule.
# Installed to: /etc/dnf/libdnf5-plugins/actions.d/kldload-be.actions by firstboot.
# Requires the libdnf5-plugin-actions package (firstboot installs it on dnf5).
#
# Role: snapshot the ZFS root boot environment before every dnf5 transaction —
#   the dnf5 peer of the dnf4 kldload_be.py plugin and the apt/pacman hooks, all
#   calling the same helper, so a bad `dnf upgrade` is a ZFSBootMenu rollback
#   rather than a reinstall. dnf5 (Fedora 41+) dropped the dnf4 Python plugin API,
#   so the EL plugin cannot work here — this actions file is the replacement.
#
# Line format (libdnf5 actions): callback:pkg_filter:direction:options:command
#   Five colon-separated fields; empty filter/direction/options = fire on EVERY
#   transaction. snapshot-create.sh exits 0 on a non-ZFS root, so this never
#   blocks an update. No raise_error option — a snapshot hiccup must not abort dnf.
# Consequence if missing: dnf5 transactions take NO labelled pre-tx BE snapshot;
#   you fall back to the coarser hourly auto/sanoid streams.
pre_transaction::::/usr/local/sbin/snapshot-create.sh dnf-pre
